{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/812987-session-zero-report-climbing-the-ladder","id":812987,"title":"Session Zero Report: Climbing the Ladder","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T16:18:11-08:00","id":812987,"title":"Session Zero Report: Climbing the Ladder","content":"My players Climbed the Ladder last session. I'm so excited about what happened, I'm gonna share the details with y'all here. The game is set in London, 1587, as written up in the Dark Eras Kickstarter PDF.<br /> <br /> The player characters who showed up were:<br /> <br /> Callum &quot;Mac&quot; MachPhearson, a minor Scottish noble unliving in London. Was big into game hunting, and a member of an exclusive cell of Hunters. Gangrel Invictus<br /> Peregrine, the only member of the party who wasn't born a noble. Operates as a fixer/favor broker for the Weihan Cynn. Daeva.<br /> Mistress Katherine, the owner and manager of a brothel. Trades blood for favors. Ventrue Invictus<br /> <br /> The NPCs...<br /> <br /> As mentioned, <b>Mac</b> once belonged to a <b>Hunting Club</b>, which he <i>abandoned</i> once he was Embraced. The club is managed by a patron with a secret identity...<br /> <br /> <b>Bartholomew Blackstone</b> is a Beast who controls the Hunting Club. Originally he used it to sate his Hunger for Prey, but now he's been co-opted by a more powerful predator. Mac once asked Blackstone for a big favor thinking that Blackstone was human, and afterwards Blackstone revealed his true nature. Mac feels like he's made a deal with the devil.<br /> <br /> <b>Edward &quot;Ned&quot; the Stableboy</b> works for Mac's estate. Ned looks up to Mac, and Mac exploits the kid by using him as bait in his hunts.<br /> <br /> <b>Hugo</b> is another Kindred who was once a noble. Hugo disgusts Mac: Hugo lazes about, and has clearly fallen into a gluttonous rut. Mac hopes that he is never like that. However, Hugo wants something from the Hunting Club.<br /> <br /> <b>Woodhouse</b> is Mac's manservant, retainer, and attach\u00e9. Mac hasn't revealed the identities of any other vampires, but Mac suspects Katherine is a Kindred.<br /> <br /> Mac wasn't sired by Invictus leader <b>Richard Bithewaye</b>, but he looks up to Richard as the ideal vampire: Power for power's sake, and unassailable. Richard is the one manipulating Blackstone. Peregrine also owes Richard <i>big</i>.<br /> <br /> Peregine once killed a man, and discovered a 4-year old. He couldn't bring himself to leave the child alone on the streets, so he took it in to raise. That was 7 years ago. Peregrine tries to keep the <b>Orphan</b> from the Requiem, but the child already suspects Mac is something <i>else</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>John</b> once worked with Peregrine. But after a heist gone wrong that Peregrine barely managed to save the two of them from, Peregrine abandoned him.<br /> <br /> <b>Ida</b> is a fellow Daeva in the Weihan Cynn that loves (or at least thinks she loves) Peregrine. He exploits her love to use her as a gopher.<br /> <br /> Peregrine's sire is a mysterious power broker known only as <b>\u03a3\u03b1\u03c4\u03b1\u03bd\u03ac\u03c2</b>. Few know this, but <b>\u03a3\u03b1\u03c4\u03b1\u03bd\u03ac\u03c2</b> respects only one other: the Blood Queen of the Weihan Cynn.<br /> <br /> <b>Agnes </b>represents what is at stake for Peregrine. She once was very much like him, until she got too greedy and began losing her contacts and allies. Now she's a shadow of her former self, desperately clinging on to the few contacts she maintains. Agnes once fooled Mac with her boasts, and currently bribes Katherine for information.<br /> <br /> <b>James Fuller</b> represents Peregrine's greatest failure: poor information got him killed.<br /> <br /> <b>Bess</b> is one of Katherine's girls. Katherine once confessed what had happened to Bess, and swore her to secrecy. Bess suspects the 4th Player Character, an English Nobleman, is a vampire as well. She also will avenge James Fuller when she discovers who his killer is.<br /> <br /> Katherine loves having the power to control minds, but she doesn't believe in brute force: much better to manipulate things subtly. There are fewer loose ends left over. Because of this, she fears becoming like <b>Mordred Killgrave</b>, another Ventrue. Killgrave abuses his powers of Dominate and refuses to improve his &quot;mundane&quot; manipulation skills. Unbeknownst to the coterie, Blackstone is cashing in major favors owed to him by Killgrave.<br /> <br /> Nobody knew his name, but Katherine discovered that one of her regulars was a hunter. She ate him and thought that the issue was solved. <b>Samuel</b> however was a member of the <b>Hunting Club</b>, who is looking for his killer.<br /> <br /> Katherine grew up on the streets before being found by her maker, <b>Mistress Ambrose</b>. Katherine had a support network at the time, though. She grew up with a group of other <b>Orphans</b>. Coincidentally, the Hunting Club has begun using orphans as an invisible spy network. They hope that the children, lacking the shame of adults, will more honestly report strange sightings.<br /> <br /> Y'all can obviously see that my players have little fear of referencing other media, or being a little silly, but even though we're only halfway finished with the Ladder, and haven't even included one of the PCs, it's pretty exciting. What do y'all think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}